# Release-path pin tuple: the versions the publish path must agree on.
#
# Read only through scripts/lib/release-pins.sh, which validates this file
# lexically before sourcing it: blank lines, comments, and these nine
# assignments, nothing else. Enforced against the tree by
# scripts/check-release-pins.sh rules 7 and 10, so a bump here cannot leave a
# copy behind.
#
# TWINE_VERSION is not a free choice: it is the twine that
# pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish bundles at PYPI_PUBLISH_ACTION_SHA
# (requirements/runtime.txt at PYPI_PUBLISH_ACTION_VERSION). Bumping the action
# means re-reading that file and moving TWINE_VERSION with it, or the local gate
# stops standing in for the upload.
#
# JSR_VERSION is the jsr CLI the publish step runs through npx; GORELEASER_VERSION
# is the goreleaser the goreleaser-action installs (its own pin is the action SHA).
#
# NPM_VERSION is the npm the publish jobs install before publishing: OIDC trusted
# publishing needs >= 11.5.1, and the Node the runner ships may be older. It is
# read here rather than written into each job so the version lives in one place.
#
# GO_VERSION is the Go the module declares and every Go job runs: the same value
# appears as the `go` directive in packages/sdk-go/go.mod, as the go-version of
# every setup-go, and as the `go${GO_VERSION}` those jobs assert `go env
# GOVERSION` against. Rule 10 holds them together, so raising the floor is one
# edit here plus the directive, never a hunt through the workflows.
#
# Refreshed as part of every release pre-flight.

NPM_VERSION=12.0.2
PIP_VERSION=26.2.1
BUILD_VERSION=1.5.0
TWINE_VERSION=7.0.0
JSR_VERSION=0.14.3
PYPI_PUBLISH_ACTION_VERSION=v1.14.2
PYPI_PUBLISH_ACTION_SHA=dc37677b2e1c63e2034f94d8a5b11f265b73ba33
GORELEASER_VERSION=v2.18.0
GO_VERSION=1.26.6
